{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/26647-abyssals-a-new-take","id":26647,"title":"Abyssals, a new take","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Abyssal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-09T12:22:17-08:00","id":26647,"title":"Abyssals, a new take","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/24407-brainstorming-introduction-exalted-webcomic/page5\">I wrote up a rant about Abyssals, and why I don't like them.</a><br /> <br /> For ease, I'll put it here:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> I guess, since I said I would, I should talk a little bit about Abyssals.<br /> <br /> Whereas I don't like like Solars because they are a good concept that just doesn't work out quite right, devolving more into Mary Sue territory... Abyssals just start out bad and get worse.<br /> <br /> First, they're a corrupted Solar. Great, now they have the flaws that Solars have as characters but<i> without any of the redeeming qualities. </i>Everyone hates you, and it's for a good reason this time...<i>because you're a horrible human being.</i> But fine, if you want to play an unrepentant villain and just revel in your dark evilness of darkness, fine. That's not my playstyle, but okay have fun. Be a supervillain. Go. Have fun.<br /> <br /> <i>But then you try to be an anti-hero. </i>Oh gods. First off, anti-heroes aren't appealing to me in the first place, so you're going to have to be really good at pulling it off from the get-go. Exactly how am I supposed to sympathize with you when you go around murdering and looting with free abandon? You're a &quot;designated hero.&quot; The only way I know that you're the hero of the story is because the story says you are. Usually by making the villain worse somehow, and with the bodycounts steadily rising from the &quot;hero&quot; and the villain....at this point I just want to stand up and walk away from the table.<br /> <br /> I suppose you could play a redemption Abyssal...but then it's kinda like just playing a Solar in emo makeup. They don't need more emo makeup.<br /> <br /> And on that thread, we've got that Abyssals used to be Solars. <i>That just makes everything worse. </i>What is trying to be said is that &quot;In each Solar is this thread of darkness.&quot; Except what is actually said is &quot;Here's the evil Solars, and there's the good Solars.&quot; This just makes the &quot;good&quot; Solars more insufferable, because <i>they</i> aren't Abyssals, QED they must be in the right, and that's what the story reinforces! The selection of Solar shards to become Abyssals being random would have been okay, if it seemed to have any sort of impact on the aesthetics and storylines at all. Instead, it just seems to be the &quot;bad&quot; Solars that spoiled the Solar barrel and gave them all a bad name, bringing us back to the &quot;unfairly persecuted&quot; Mary Sue Solars.<br /> <br /> <br /> I see Solars as a good idea that just needs a bit of tweaking to distance themselves from the Mary Sue territory they dug themselves into.<br /> <br /> Abyssals...I don't even know <i>how</i> to fix Abyssals. I can't even ignore them because even them <i>existing</i> taints the interesting aspects of the Solars. I guess the only way would be to make them their entire new thing, completely separate from Solars. But I don't see that happening.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> They can be a decent villain splat, (if a bit emo,) but really, they fail in any other aspect. And in an world trying to be complex and well-rounded in its views....this one-dimensional Exaltation really falls flat. (har har.)<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The main points are:<br /> <br /> 1. They are a one-dimensional villain splat<br /> 2. They are bleak darkness of dark darkitude.<br /> 3. Their relationship with Solars detracts from Solar story, and does not add.<br /> <br /> Feel free to disagree with me, but that's not the point of this thread. Instead, it is inspired by my closing statement: &quot;Abyssals...I don't even know <i>how</i> to fix Abyssals.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Or in other words....<br /> <br /> <i>Challenge Accepted.</i><br /> <hr /><br /> When the Sun first set his foot down upon Creation, his might and grace radiated from him, that even his formless shadow became a God in its own right.<br /> <br /> It is a terrible lesson that should be considered: The Sun, in his marvelous glory, is so overpowering that he even gives form and shape simply from his <i>absence</i>. Is it then, surprising, that such a thing would happen when he created his Chosen?<br /> <br /> When the Sun imparted just a <i>piece</i> of his glory into these glorious shards, the shadows he cast were also formed: everything the Solar <i>was not.</i> They fled his light into the darkest reaches they could to avoid his gaze, eventually finding the Void, that space of non-existence created when the Primordials forged Creation out the Wyld.<br /> <br /> These shadows of the Solar Exalted would have remained entrapped in this realm of non-existence, if not for the foolishness and pride of the Exalted host. They first trapped the hungering spirits of the dead Primordials--the Neverborn--into the Void to be disposed of and forgotten, bringing that faint spark of existence into the Void. And then, worse, <i>they woke it up.</i><br /> <br /> The Neverborn hungered for revenge, to eat away at the world and reality so denied to them. They searched the formless Void and found these shadows of the Solar Exalted, and with their stolen secrets, forged their own Exalted from the shadows of the Sun's own designs. They toiled in their unreality, bringing each and every one to their designs (what did they care of the Law of Diminishment? How can you diminish something that no longer exists?) and then released them upon Creation with one singular goal: <b>Consume.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> The Neverborn guide these Abyssal exaltations upon mortals, just as the Sun chooses his own Solars. However, as a hollow mockery they choose those that are weak, who seek power in greed, and who utterly fail in their moment of glory. Oh, those chosen are great, but they are also terrible and loathsome, antithetical to everything the Sun strives for.<br /> <br /> The power comes upon the mortal much as the Solar's does: unbidden and unasked for. The Shadows and the powers of the Void seep into her soul, empowering her darkest desires. For some, they feel a strong resonance with this unending emptiness, willing to consume and destroy all they wish, just as the Neverborn desired.<br /> <br /> However, most mortals quell at such power, shaken by the Void that now taints them. They are given new light upon their own destructive nature, and when faced with the sheer consumption of unreality--shirk. But many still fall into the base desires of the Void, enticed by the darkness and simply not strong enough to avoid its gnawing hunger. Often, these people will try to sate their thirst, targeting those that--in their eyes--deserve to die. Those that prey on the weak, those that slay as the first group of Abyssals would.<br /> <br /> And yet, there are those that, when looking into the mouth of the Void within them, realize how precious life truly is. They fight against the darkness in their hearts, clawing at what remains of their life, protecting others, teaching them to appreciate what already exists. Only they truly know what <i>nothing</i> is, and so will fight to keep <i>anything</i> alive.<br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> Still a few problems, but I think it makes them more well-rounded and less one-dimensional. Even though we've still got &quot;loyalist, anti-hero, renagade,&quot; it feels more even in its execution. It keeps ties with Solars, but doesn't force them to be the &quot;fallen&quot; Solars. They were created this way from the beginning. They are <i>starting</i> from the darkness. They can move to the &quot;light&quot; just as a Solar can move into &quot;darkness.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T12:32:59-08:00","id":26650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Still a few problems, but I think it makes them more well-rounded and less one-dimensional. Even though we've still got &quot;loyalist, anti-hero, renagade,&quot; it feels more even in its execution. </div> </div> </div>Not really, no. It is functionally no broader than canon Abyssals, and in fact less so due to the mandate that your character have been weak, cowardly, greedy, or a failure. It also gives personal agency to the Neverborn, and removes the deathlords from the equation entirely. All in all, it is worse than what we currently have.<br /> <br /> It seems the problems highlighted in your opening quote would be best solved by talking to people who <i>actually played Abyssals. </i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T12:35:03-08:00","id":26656,"title":"","content":"Fair enough. Just a writing exercise to get ideas out of my head if nothing else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T12:56:20-08:00","id":26681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1. They are a one-dimensional villain splat<br /> 2. They are bleak darkness of dark darkitude. </div> </div> </div>I personally think that a lot of these problems are the direct result of their 'creators' the Neverborn/Oblivion. Infernals are created by the Yozis who, while admittedly static in personality as a baseline, present a wide range of motifs and themes to don. The Neverborn have one goal, one motif, one outlook, which leads their Exalted progeny to look samey and uninteresting.<br /> <br /> I think in giving the Neverborn even more agency/control you end up exacerbating the problems you list, especially since Deathlords now don't seem to be part of the equation? I have my own problems with the Deathlords as presented so far, but they at least provide some buffer from the overly simplistic Neverborn.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Doh, Omicron got there faster...and used the same 'equation' language I did, so he's probably a double witch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":870,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/870-side-item","user":"Side Item","date":". 12-09-2013, 03:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/870-side-item","name":"Side Item","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar870_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T13:20:42-08:00","id":26692,"title":"","content":"Oh no! People don't like my hastily-written up, caffeine-induced solution to a entrenched and horribly complex problem! My ego!<br /> <br /> Let's try to make it better.<br /> <br /> First off: yes, I don't like Abyssals and don't play them, so as someone that plays them, what is it you like and enjoy about them?<br /> <br /> So, let's look at some of my ideas and argue with them, try to hash it out. Let's feel free to throw out nearly everything canon and start anew. Here's a few notes I was focusing on in this attempt.<br /> <br /> 1. Let's keep that the Solars and Abyssals are related somehow. However, I don't like the idea that they're <i>corrupted</i> Solars. It starts off the conversation of &quot;good&quot; and &quot;bad.&quot; We want Abyssals be dark and of the Void, not necessarily evil.<br /> <br /> 2. The Void doesn't necessarily need to be all death and destruction. It is absence, it is wanting to be filled, which, in its mindlessness often <i>means</i> destruction, but not necessarily. Maybe you fill that void with care of others, with trying to make the world a better place because you know what emptiness is. That distinction leaves people much more open right away.<br /> <br /> 3. Yeah, the seeking of exaltation didn't work. Let's just throw that out for now. Any ideas what the chosen of the Void would be attracted to in Exaltation qualities?<br /> <br /> 4. Neverborn being too active and the Deathlords. I dunno, see, I don't like the Deathlords because it reinforces the idea that &quot;Only Solars can do anything ever, even when dead.&quot; Sure, the Deathlords are powerful tools and certainly guide the Chosen of the Void, but shouldn't the ultimate power come from the Neverborn themselves, even if it is aimless? As well, I like the idea that the Neverborn can't create anything at all, hence the shadows of the Solar Exaltations. They didn't create those shadows, they just took what the Sun accidentally created.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T13:38:21-08:00","id":26704,"title":"","content":"While I do agree with the above, that concern only matters when considering the current idea of the Neverborn, rather than what they could possibly be. What is a Primordial? The condensation of a concept into a spiritual form, from which tangential aspects cascade. What is a Neverborn? A dead concept. What is a dead concept? That is a trickier question.<br /> <br /> Is it, perhaps, an idea which no one ever considers? Can such a completely abandoned idea even exist, when believers in a flat Earth still existed in our own world not so long ago? Is it instead like a dead language, an idea which is no longer used and does not change, but is only observed? Given the stupendous power of the Exalted, is it a gaping hole in reality where something used to be? Is is an inversion, the inside of a mask like the Underworld compared to Creation? That last one perhaps holds some value, as the death of one Primordial brought life to the region where its body fell. In the end, it doesn't really matter, does it? They all <i>might</i> work, so you might as well throw them in there as campaign hooks.<br /> <br /> In any case, the goal of Abyssals is to kill Creation. But how does one kill a world? Tossing it into the Void is the easy way, but I don't much suppose beings trapped in eternal agony care how it's done, so much as someone gets it done soon, what with those idiot Deathlords wasting five thousand years. So apply any of the above methods of killing an idea to killing the world. Perhaps Who Holds in Thrall would be able to pass if you killed all names, which of course would require murdering Swillin as well and thus creating a new Neverborn, but c'est la vie.<br /> <br /> I just want my colorful Dia de los Muertos Abyssals already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm working on it, all right?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/130-gensh","name":"Gensh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar130_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"128"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T14:03:03-08:00","id":26719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh no! People don't like my hastily-written up, caffeine-induced solution to a entrenched and horribly complex problem! My ego!<br /> Let's try to make it better. </div> </div> </div>FWIW, I wasn't going for a bashing tone in my response, and apologize if that style of tone was apparent at all.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1. Let's keep that the Solars and Abyssals are related somehow. However, I don't like the idea that they're corrupted Solars. It starts off the conversation of &quot;good&quot; and &quot;bad.&quot; We want Abyssals be dark and of the Void, not necessarily evil. </div> </div> </div>I think this is most easily solved by just never using &quot;corrupted&quot; to describe what happens. Just use variations of 'change' and keep it mostly neutral.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. The Void doesn't necessarily need to be all death and destruction. It is absence, it is wanting to be filled, which, in its mindlessness often means destruction, but not necessarily. Maybe you fill that void with care of others, with trying to make the world a better place because you know what emptiness is. That distinction leaves people much more open right away. </div> </div> </div>I agree, somewhat. Making Abyssals the Exalted of Murder led to a lot of effects that were basically bad black Magic the Gathering cards, i.e. &quot;Do [X] like a Solar would, and as an additional cost sacrifice a creature.&quot;<br /> <br /> However, I think making them Exalted of the Void is sort of circling the same idea. I do think that their powers should easily lend to lessening Creation, but I've always felt that Abyssals should emulate the Underworld more (overall bad for Creation, although not de facto so) rather than the Void/Oblivion (which, as you pointed out, is just <b>Consume</b>).<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4. Neverborn being too active and the Deathlords. I dunno, see, I don't like the Deathlords because it reinforces the idea that &quot;Only Solars can do anything ever, even when dead.&quot; Sure, the Deathlords are powerful tools and certainly guide the Chosen of the Void, but shouldn't the ultimate power come from the Neverborn themselves, even if it is aimless? As well, I like the idea that the Neverborn can't create anything at all, hence the shadows of the Solar Exaltations. They didn't create those shadows, they just took what the Sun accidentally created. </div> </div> </div>I think this problem is better solved by reworking the Deathlords rather than beefing up the Neverborn. In the abstract, I think I'm on the same page as to the current Deathlord's problems. As it is, the Deathlords are 13 giant bowling balls in the rubber sheet that is the Underworld; Everything ends up getting sucked into their gravity, or having to justify how they stay out of the event horizon.<br /> <br /> BUT, removing their influence just moves Abyssals closer to Exalted of the Void, which as I said I view as being kissing cousins with Exalted of Murder. Plus, losing Deathlords lessens both the apprentice-master experience and the opportunity of getting sucked up in the passion operas fueled by centuries old grudges.<br /> <br /> If you're going to throw out canon/rework things from the beginning, I'd personally start by saying that the Neverborn are truly dead/exist only as aimless Whispers of the Labyrinth, and that the Deathlord concept dives into the 1E core blurb of &quot;thousands of petty dictators fighting eternally amongst themselves and their passion plays&quot;. That way you can have deathknights be more focused on their individual Deathlords, which offers more idiosyncratic potential, rather than Oblivion.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/870-side-item","name":"Side Item","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar870_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T14:11:27-08:00","id":26725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Side Item</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/26647-abyssals-a-new-take?p=26719#post26719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">FWIW, I wasn't going for a bashing tone in my response, and apologize if that style of tone was apparent at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was just making fun of myself! I didn't feel offended. (Just a little crestfallen, unreasonably so. Basically: &quot;Oh no, people didn't instantly love something I was throwing out in the heat of the moment without reworking!&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T14:11:51-08:00","id":26726,"title":"","content":"I think a part of the problem is that the concept of an afterlife is a familiar, comfortable one to most of the Western world. Death is a transition to another state of existence, death is a natural thing, and so by extension, the transition to that other state of existence is also relatively natural. We have gods that act as guides to the recently dead, visitable afterlives, and the kingdom of the dead as a part of the natural order. From Greece's Elysian Fields, to the Maitlands and the Deetzes learning to get along, to Demi Moore and Patrick Swazye spinning a wheel post-mortem; we have a consistent refrain of the living and the dead finding a peaceful co-existence. Even with the counterexamples (often in the same media!) it's presented as a balance and a natural thing.<br /> <br /> A lot of us also have enough familiarity with Buddhism to understand Nirvana as the kind of complete ego annihilation that the Void seems to promise and which the Neverborn nominally seek. Surcease of suffering; the final balm in Gilead.<br /> <br /> This is also why you see a lot of people that try and soften Abyssals by pushing towards 'Solars of the Underworld'. To make them the psychopomps, the guardians of the good death, the destroyer of those things whose time has come. A turning of violence towards good purpose.<br /> <br /> Thing is, there *is* an Exalt type of psychopomps, guardians of the good death and the destroyer of things whose time has come. The Chosen of Endings.<br /> <br /> The Underworld in Exalted isn't meant to be part of the natural order- it's meant to be a *horrifying abberration* of that order. An awful and terrible thing. It's the antithesis of the good death- it's the thing that's lingered on past it's time. Nothing wholesome for the living of Creation should arise from the Underworld. This is why there are no natural gods of the Underworld, nor does Heaven try and extend it's domain thereupon. This is why everything that draws on necrotic essence is inherently a Creature of Darkness. The Underworld isn't where things go to die, or even where things go when they've died- it's where things go when they should be gone but *aren't*.<br /> <br /> The hardest part for making interesting Abyssals isn't in contrast with the Solars- they don't actually share that much conceptual space in my experience, save as people choose to play it up. The hard part is making reasonable and sympathetic Abyssals that don't end up looking like Reckoners with darker and edgier makeup.<br /> <br /> (Sidenote: A lot of this is the result of pondering some comments that Holden and Hatewheel made over time, which have caused me to re-consider my thinking on both the Underworld and the Abyssals. It still is likely not right!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T14:12:27-08:00","id":26727,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think the write-up in the first post here doesn't give even the 2e Abyssals book enough credit. I'll try and put down what I see as core design conceits for an Abyssals splat in a poorly-worded and rambling form, as it's finals week for me. I agree with some of the issues; They should not be one-dimensional villains, and I really don't see the need for them to be emo, though I think just how dead you are inside should be something of an issue for many Abyssals. I've played Abyssals for a long time at this point with a big group of great players, and I think that I've got a handle on how I'd like the splat to go that isn't too terrible.<br /> <br /> 1. Hardly anybody knows what you are.<br /> <br /> Solars existed historically and get spoken about by the Immaculate Order and the secret Cult of the Illuminated. Sidereals know all about Solars. Lunars probably have an oral history of Solars. Infernals have a peerage in Hell, and tend to be closely associated with certain types of demons, giving them at least a certain resemblance to the &quot;Crazy Akuma Solars&quot; that existed during history, and in my opinion, they should have more superficial/appearance based similarities to Solars.<br /> <br /> Abyssals are probably some weird form of Anathema to anyone who follows the Immaculate Faith, but outside of Lookshy, the splat's hardly had time to develop a reputation and history in a world where most of the population is illiterate. It may be pretty obvious after some time that you're a weird sort of Death Exalt, maybe the world's strongest Ghost-Blooded, but what exactly you do is largely a legend you create that relies on no existing precedent. Whether you're a bad guy or a scary good guy or a weird guy whose appearance tends to coincide with bad people spontaneously turning into mincemeat, well, you'll define that in your story.<br /> <br /> 2. Liminals are Ghost Hunters now? Well, you're a Ghost Brother.<br /> <br /> What are Ghosts in Creation? They're the ones who didn't or couldn't pass into Lethe and reincarnate because they had unfinished business, wanted more out of life, or just weren't ready. Well, your Exaltation is just like that, except it's backed by the power of a Solar shard and done under the tutelage of the nigh-almighty Deathlords. Maybe, in 3E, Ghosts can be made to not be completely dull and weak and actually comprise an interesting group of millions to be involved with. This opens up tons of plot potential, as virtually everyone you know in your knew life as some form of unfinished business, or some axe to grind before they go, and nobody walks between the two worlds quite as casually or as dangerously as you do.<br /> <br /> On this note, I think Abyssals have a lot of room to develop &quot;charms&quot; that key off of the fact that they are pretty much the only beings in Creation that have died and come back to life, and this opens up space for tons of powers that aren't straight copy-paste jobs of Solar powers; While I love the connection to Solars, I hate the Mirror keyword with a passion 99% of the time. During the other 1%, there's an interesting and thematic difference between the Abyssal and Solar version of the Charm.<br /> <br /> 3. You're a Ghost Sister, the Deathlords are Mom and Dad, and they're not so different from you.<br /> <br /> The Deathlords died after having what was, from their perspective, history's greatest injustice perpetrated against them. They refused to go away and made a pact with forces from beyond to become powerful enough to exact justice. That's probably a lot like your story, and at least one of the Deathlords probably has a story that matches up very closely to your reasons for sticking around and not just trying your luck next time as a squirrel. In addition to having some of the most powerful tutors in the setting teaching you how to be as much of a badass as possible, you're also learning about who some real assholes are, people who are responsible for the kind of things that make you angry. And, all of a sudden, you're very scary when you're angry.<br /> <br /> 4. Avenging Angels aren't necessarily bad guys.<br /> <br /> When you're released into Creation, you have lots of room to do good things, and even the Deathlords are probably pushing you on that path to some extent. The people you take down are typically going to have done terrible things, the kind of things people can't forget even after millennia in Stygia. Your stance on collateral damage and whatever side activities you take are largely up to you.<br /> <br /> The nature of your powers and the neuroses you carry with you (see Shard's Dark Fate) will, though, ensure that the methods you use to take people down tend to be rather destructive. Exigent of Yo Ping, sadly, you aren't.<br /> <br /> 5. There's more than one way to go from here.<br /> <br /> I see at least three clear and distinct options for an Abyssal at this point. One, usually reserved for NPCs but interesting in the hands of the right player, involves becoming so radicalized that they fully back the mission of the Neverborn and want to see the world end, not in the paltry sense of the Ebon Dragon overthrowing the ruling order, but truly bringing about an end to everything. Pulling an Abyssal like this back from the brink can serve for an amazing story, and in the process, the Deathlords themselves may even debate their long term purpose. The second option is to be an Abyssal, but try to walk the tightrope of humanity, remaking the world into what you view as a better, more just place with your destructive powers. Trying to be true to your identity both as an Abyssal and as a human. Lastly, you've got those who can't take the destructive methods any longer, those Compassion 5 types who seek to escape the Abyss entirely, or others who end up considering the state of themselves and their Deathlord masters to be the greatest trick the Primordials ever pulled. These characters may seek redemption for themselves, and they may seek to get their friends, and perhaps even their Deathlord, out of the grip of the Neverborn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1595,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1595-scatters-the-ashes","user":"Scatters-the-Ashes","date":". 12-09-2013, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1595-scatters-the-ashes","name":"Scatters-the-Ashes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1595_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T14:49:31-08:00","id":26747,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry, Dragonmystic, but I am almost as put off by your take on Abyssals as you are of the normals take on Abyssals. And I'm trying to think of why. Maybe it's the fact that I actually enjoyed playing normal Abyssals both in redemptionist, and blatantly nihilistic antihero/villain forms. Perhaps it's something about how you still needed to use a Solar Exaltation to explain where the Abyssals came from, when the Primordial War and the very idea of Exaltation as a weapon capable of slaying the Makers of All Creation usually feels like enough. I'mm not sure. But until I get to the bottom of this, I'm going to keep rereading this. Because usually, I enjoy hearing your arguments. So this.... this is perplexing the begebus out of me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T15:22:29-08:00","id":26759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brasstreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/26647-abyssals-a-new-take?p=26747#post26747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because usually, I enjoy hearing your arguments. So this.... this is perplexing the begebus out of me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't worry about it, I'm not really happy with it either; this is not my best work. I think I wrote this as an outlet for frustration and anger, rather than an actual argument or attempt to make things for Abyssals.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T15:54:47-08:00","id":26776,"title":"","content":"I think what bugs me about Abyssals can be summed up thusly:<br /> <br /> 1. Dark Fate<br /> <br /> If the Neverborn can make people spontaneously up and die in Creation, then why the hell aren't they doing this all the time, all day, everyday? I get that the gameplay reason is to drive home a &quot;damned if you do/damned if you don't&quot; mentality, but it really limits the stories you can tell with an Abyssal to &quot;emo&quot; or &quot;murderhobo&quot;.<br /> <br /> Now as every use of Necromancy drags the Void into Creation, I'd much rather see every Abyssal get the Necromancy induction Charms for free (once they meet the minimum Essence requirements). I'd like to see Abyssals burdened by a more traditional Limit Break that drives them to Nihilism, making their Frenzy mechanic more personal (&quot;what have I done!&quot;) and less about untouchable NPC characters (&quot;rocks fall, all your loved ones die&quot;).<br /> <br /> 2. The ****ing Deathlords<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong. The Deathlords are interesting. Working for a Deathlord Liege is interesting. Sacrificing freedom for power is interesting. (And as far as 3rd Ed is concerned: learning the custom charms of a First Age superbeing is interesting.) What is not interesting, is if you have <i>no choice</i> but to play these stories. The Deathlords define the Deathknights: either your character is ruled by a Deathlord, or is ruled by their opposition of their Deathlord. (And as far as 3rd ed is concerned, if your only path to character development is becoming more like your Deathlord then that's 2nd Ed's Infernals-Yozi problem all over again.)<br /> <br /> Now if Deathlords were powerful rulers among the dead, and Deathknights are the champions of the dead we have a more interesting dynamic than the Massa/Slave set up we have now. Remove the leash from the hands of the Deathlords and have Abyssals choose whether or not to deal with the Deathlords <i>on their own terms</i>. Now the mechanics of Exaltation can stay pretty much the same, great power offered to people on the verge of death. Maybe it's the Whispers of the Neverborn that offer Exaltation or Death. Maybe Deathlords can sense when a mortal is about to Exalt as an Abyssal and come to give a big speech and potentially pick up a new recruit... but it's all bluster and no substance. Monstrances can stay but their power needs to be neutered: they shouldn't be a shock collar or a kill switch, they should be a liability - a paper fetter holding down a god.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> With these changes, they're not &quot;a one-dimensional villain splat&quot;: they are the Exalted of Death, capable of telling whatever stories they want to tell. They might still be the &quot;bleak darkness of dark darkitude&quot;, as their themes will still be death and nothingness, but it's a darkness put firmly in the players hands - no more NPCs gimping your loved ones no more being press ganged into Team Kill-The-World. Their relationship with Solars is that of a dark mirror. Now you could argue that this doesn't add anything to the Solar mythos and screws over the design space of Evil Solars, but by putting agency in the players hands instead of setting in stone in a sourcebook, you can play any Solar concept as an Abyssal. There won't be a Redemption or Destruction dichotomy, and instead Abyssals will get to play whatever they want to be in whichever shade of grey they like... just like Solars. Which would actually let your explore the theme that Abyssals are !Solars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 12-09-2013, 07:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T15:54:56-08:00","id":26777,"title":"","content":"I really like that they're so dark and evil and villanous and just terrible people who do terrible things because they're awful. That actually appeals to me.<br /> <br /> Although, I have to say, I really enjoy your version of the origin of the Abyssal Exaltation. It removes that whole notion of an abyssal &quot;taint&quot; on otherwise pristine Solar Shards, makes them wholly of the darkness, and I really like that. For them, there is no redemption, and there's a lot less angst, too. They're not corrupted and twisted heroes with a chance at righteousness that they don't know they have. They're born in darkness and their powers channel that darkness.<br /> <br /> Getting rid of the abyssal taint notion, there's not as much of an imperative to have them pervert and destroy everything of Creation. They don't do it because they're angst-ridden emo-Solars. They do it because that is their very nature. But, as you wrote, they have some say in the matter. They could say, &quot;fuck that! I may be stuck as a creature of darkness with abyssal powers, but I don't have to use them so literally. I can be creative. I can use them to help. If I can't build a better world, I can tear down an awful one so that others can build in its place.&quot;<br /> <br /> Framing makes a big difference in my opinion, and the way you've framed this changes things in a subtle but important way.<br /> <br /> <br /> ... and just to note, I also find the idea of tainted Solars somewhat appealing, too. I'm good either way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T16:36:02-08:00","id":26809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/26647-abyssals-a-new-take?p=26777#post26777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... and just to note, I also find the idea of tainted Solars somewhat appealing, too. I'm good either way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the status quo because the breaking of the Jade Prison makes sense this way.<br /> <br /> If you change where Abyssals come from, you pretty much have to throw out the canon explanation as to why the Solars are back. Which might work for you: some people like a bit of mystery and homebrew in their settings. But I would prefer is 3rd didn't run quite so roughshod over the established story of Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T16:40:37-08:00","id":26811,"title":"","content":"This version of the Abyssal Origin doesn't have to impact on why the Solars have returned. It requires a bit of tweaking. Perhaps the Yozis sent a Second or Third Circle Demon to open the Jade Prison and it only managed to snag 50 Exaltations before someone was able to banish it back to Malfeas. Maybe in this story, the Yozis managed to capture more than just 50 of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T16:57:46-08:00","id":26825,"title":"","content":"Personally, I think &quot;terrible people who do terrible things&quot; can be, well, any splat. We've got Lunar Elders, First Age and Sig solars, countless Terrestrials, a good portion of Infernals, and, in their own way, plenty of Sidereals who can fit that mold. Making a splat where everyone is terrible and does terrible things seems, to me, to be a terrible idea. If you know you're going to be a terrible person and do terrible things every time you play the splat, that pretty much takes all the drama out of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1595-scatters-the-ashes","name":"Scatters-the-Ashes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1595_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T16:58:48-08:00","id":26826,"title":"","content":"&quot;Terrible people who do terrible things&quot; pretty much describes <i>It's Always Sunny in Philadelphia</i>. I love that show.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T17:04:37-08:00","id":26828,"title":"","content":"Okay, I concede that being able to be played as black comedy about powerful assholes should be a design goal for Abyssals, Infernals, and shit, most every splat. I just would feel it a waste of potential to make that the only viable option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1595-scatters-the-ashes","name":"Scatters-the-Ashes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1595_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T17:11:53-08:00","id":26838,"title":"","content":"Oh a complete waste, I agree. It's really the sort of thing that should be found on discussion forums and not in the books.<br /> <br /> So ... who wants to play a game where all the characters decide to become addicted to crack?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T17:41:15-08:00","id":26853,"title":"","content":"Abyssals are really a product of their surroundings. Solar shards corrupted by the Neverborn, infusing them with the memory of what these Neverborn see them as, murderers and defilers. So basically they're Solars changed by their original sin. This isn't what they have to be. They're first and foremost corrupted Solars, so they have the tabula rasa that Solar pcs would, except a darker tinge because they're of the Underworld. It's what they do that defines them and their powers. Some find agency with a Deathlord, others serve the Neverborn directly, many find solace in the Underworld, and others try to eke out an existence in Creation. The Underworld is as massive and, I argue, more complex than Creation, for it contains the history of existence since the death of the first Primordials. It is a clot in the cycle of reincarnation, a place of permanence and memory, tainted by the nightmares of the sleeping dead Neverborn and their desire to die manifesting as Oblivion. An Abyssal can do all manner of things, like a Solar, but their tale is likely of tragedy, not heroism, for they're intrinsically corrupted by the first deaths of the Neverborn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T22:26:03-08:00","id":27004,"title":"","content":"Why not open the Abyssal Experience to ALL the Chosen? <br /> <br /> What if, instead of being intentionally corrupted Solar Essences, any and all Exaltations are capable of being tainted by the darkness of the Neverborn equally (I dunno how, maybe hanging around in Shadowlands too long)? What if &quot;Abyssal Exalted&quot; refers to ANY Death-aspected Exalted, with &quot;Deathknights&quot; being Dark Solars, &quot;Deathseers&quot; being Dark Sids, &quot;Deathbeasts&quot; being Dark Lunars, etc?<br /> <br /> While we're at it, the Deathlords could also be opened up to other Chosen types...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T02:56:13-08:00","id":27092,"title":"","content":"@Hand: If you do that, though, Abyssal-ness turns into a D&amp;D template as opposed to an Exalt type. It would make an interesting splat, &quot;what happens when you stuff various Exalt types into the Monstrance of Celestial Easy-Bake&quot; but would be the exception as opposed to the rule. They started with 100 Solar Exaltations, and those would be their front-line weapons.<br /> <br /> 2E Abyssals noted that Lunars and Sidereals could be made into Deathlords. RotSE allows for the option of Her Redness becoming a Terrestrial Deathlord. Adding more Exalt types to the Deathlords' ranks would be a good option, I think (making the Dowager actually have been a Lunar would be a good start.)<br /> <br /> I don't think that Abyssals need a massive overhaul to be &quot;fixed,&quot; I think their background needs to be expanded to allow the players more slack with game types. A couple ideas: 1) none of this &quot;gaze into the Abyss and surrender your name to the Neverborn before you're truly Exalted&quot; BS. Every other Exaltation is a package deal, so forcing Abyssals to jump through extra hoops (with stifling background implications besides) to get to playable isn't a good thing. 2) Allow a &quot;free-range&quot; option, loose Abyssal Exaltations that simply Exalt dying mortals without any of the Deathlord whozis (the background justification would be easy. Maybe Princess Starscream destroyed her Monstrances as opposed to surrendering them. Maybe one of the more cerebral Deathlords deliberately cut some loose, just to see what sort of damage they could do by inflicting hapless schmucks with the Dark Fate. Maybe this is what happens when an Abyssal who's accepted Eternal Malevolence Enslavement suffers final death.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/739-edgewalker22","name":"edgewalker22","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar739_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T04:38:00-08:00","id":27115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>edgewalker22</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/26647-abyssals-a-new-take?p=27092#post27092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) none of this &quot;gaze into the Abyss and surrender your name to the Neverborn before you're truly Exalted&quot; BS. Every other Exaltation is a package deal, so forcing Abyssals to jump through extra hoops (with stifling background implications besides) to get to playable isn't a good thing. 2) Allow a &quot;free-range&quot; option, loose Abyssal Exaltations that simply Exalt dying mortals without any of the Deathlord whozis (the background justification would be easy. Maybe Princess Starscream destroyed her Monstrances as opposed to surrendering them. Maybe one of the more cerebral Deathlords deliberately cut some loose, just to see what sort of damage they could do by inflicting hapless schmucks with the Dark Fate. Maybe this is what happens when an Abyssal who's accepted Eternal Malevolence Enslavement suffers final death.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, somebody mentions a thought process that I've seen <i>work</i> in a campaign. There were three PCs; a loyalist Moonshadow with a Deathlord and a box, one newly-made Midnight who hadn't seen the Deathlord or the Neverborn but had a box (and was certainly a deathknight), and one 'free-range' Dusk that, unfortunately, I had to chain up in order to get him in the same room as the other two. By the end of the first session, all three of them were 'freed' Abyssals (the monstrances blew up..... how odd), but what made it interesting was how their different backgrounds made their shared state of 'freedom' so varied. The Midnight felt a pang of hope and thought this 'freed' thing was good, the Moonshadow's entire world fell apart and he started panicking like a beheaded chicken (even with the upsurge of Willpower), and the Dusk was all 'this is just the natural state of your Exaltation, why are you two reacting like this' (he never had a Monstrance, so there was no upsurge of Willpower for him).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T07:59:43-08:00","id":27195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonmystic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/26647-abyssals-a-new-take?p=26692#post26692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Yeah, the seeking of exaltation didn't work. Let's just throw that out for now. Any ideas what the chosen of the Void would be attracted to in Exaltation qualities?</div> </div> </div> </div>Being about to die, being willing to do anything to survive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}